How about:

Shieldbreaker: +0 to hit, +5 to dam, extra +5 to hit & 2x dam. against 
monters w/ armor OR weapon, no bonuses against others (acts like a
normal longsword), stops all missle attacks at you (including potions).

Mindsword: +0 to hit,+5 to dam, poison on hit, creatures one space away
must save and/or use MR otherwise be made peaceful, peaceful->tame.
Unique creatures not affected.  Taming check only done once every
five turns or so.

Wayfinder: +0 to hit, +5 to dam, finds secret doors/items/traps the
same way a helm of telepathy works, always shows the location of
the stair up/down.

Coinspinner: +5 to hit & dam, luckstone, autosearch, may teleport
to another location on the level if dropped.

Townsaver:  +0 to hit, +5 to dam., in a shop, mine town, graveyard,
tower, barraks, etc. you get +5 to hit and double speed (speed of
3 with speed boots).

Dragonslicer: +0/+5 to hit/dam., 4x damage against dragons.

Stonecutter: +0/+5, may walk through walls like an umber hulk/dwarf
/etc. does (in one turn).

Sightblinder: +0/+5, invisible, displacement, see invisible, other
creatures must save/use MR before they can attack you.

Farslayer: +0/+5, can be thrown at a creature for an instant kill,
can also be thrown back at you (use the normal t command, must still
be lined up with the target).

Doomgiver: +0/+5, reflection and MR.

Woundhealer: +0/+5, heals monsters the amount of damage rolled, harms
undead with a 2x bonus on damage, regeneration, cure sickness/blindness/
hall./confusion/etc.

Soulcutter: +0/+5, use food at 4x the rate, all monsters 1 space away
lose 2 hp/turn, you lose 1 hp/turn, drain one level on hit.


